hello everyone i'm alana and welcome to  my channel and today i am very excited  to announce that i have made the  decision  after about a year of streaming  consistently  to partner on twitch this is something  that if you've watched a lot of my  streams or  even recent q a type videos i've  toyed with the idea of it on and off for  a really long time and was very  uncertain about doing it as someone who  was previously streaming simultaneously  on  youtube twitch and facebook that meant  managing three chats and three very  different kinds of  cultures uh and eventually i decided  that  partnering on twitch made made sense and  seemed like a good idea  so first up if you're watching this  video at the moment it published i am  doing  my first ever partner stream over on  twitch  right now i published this so that it  would type out so that would be a thing  it's very exciting it's i don't know it  feels like a cool thing even though i've  had that partner invite sitting in my  inbox for about a year  it's um weirdly exciting to to to be a  part of  this thing and be like more involved in  the twitch ecosystem and be able to  squad stream with my friends and all  that stuff  so as for why i decided to do this after  streaming on multiple platforms all at  once  i previously didn't want to because i'm  generally against exclusivity deals i  think they're pretty sucky in general  and i have been on youtube for such a  long time that it didn't seem right to  leave the youtube audience and go to  another platform when i'd already built  that audience on youtube but i actually  think this will make my youtube channel  better  but okay yeah there are a bunch of  reasons first i think youtube channels  are stronger when they do edited videos  so  i will continue to have edited content  uh including the podcast  up here on youtube and we'll also take  any streams that i particularly like and  edit them down  and as a person who has never done  overlays or like you know the  sub shout outs or any of that um i don't  imagine that any of that will be in the  edited down content but for like a  stream that's two hours i plan to have  like a 15 minute highlight video  kind of thing it's also just that my  youtube has become this like weird grab  bag of different kinds of content which  is kind of intentional just as a  reminder it is a personal channel  this youtube channel is not a gaming  channel it has always been intended to  be  my personal youtube channel where i just  largely end up talking about video games  anyway  um because that's what interests me the  most but i feel like it makes more sense  to have like a more consistent  kind of content on youtube and move the  big old long streams elsewhere  um and edit them down for youtube videos  instead so they would be kind of more  similar to a fun house video i do have  some edited streams like check out my  resident evil 2 edit  i think that's a really good stream edit  i was very proud of that one i think  it's very funny  but it will be basically better youtube  content and not just big long unedited  streams where i'm like talking to chat  and stuff part of it is also  that uh because youtube has a different  culture and i did speak to other  creators about this before making this  decision  uh youtube chat is often just  a lot more negative than twitch chat i  think that's because twitch  has more of a community focus obviously  starting  a very long time ago as a streaming  website where youtube didn't and that  doesn't bother me  uh really ever but it does mean that the  youtube chat ends up with people just  arguing with each other a lot of the  time and sometimes i don't even know  what they're arguing about the youtube  chat  which has made me say on multiple  occasions for the people here who are  cool just come over to the twitch chat  instead  because the culture there is like just a  lot more fun i started to have a  preference to reading twitch chat versus  youtube chat  uh not to fault any of my youtube mods  who've done a wonderful job but just  the culture is different and like i said  i did talk to other creators and i was  like is this  like am i wrong about this and they're  like no it's 100 a thing that youtube  chat can just be a lot more toxic  all the console wars trash people get  caught up in just doesn't seem to be as  much of a thing on twitch  and i had people in my community reach  out to me and kind of tell me that over  time they had noticed that on my youtube  chat  and came over to twitch anyway to the  extent where i now when i stream have  more viewers on twitch than i do on  youtube  anyway because the good people were kind  of noticing that happening  and leaving the youtube streams part of  it is also that i have made  uh not technically but virtually zero  dollars from streaming on twitch i have  always made absolutely zero dollars no  subs  no no tips no bits i don't even know  what the lingo is  i'm that unfamiliar with this kind of  thing i do  technically sometimes get ad revenue if  i leave a youtube stream up and i am  going to make another channel um as a  sidebar  which i will leave a link to in the  description for vods for people who  don't catch twitch streams but still do  want to watch that content so i will  just upload them later on to youtube  like the next day or something uh but  ultimately as someone who  every single stream that i did in  february bar one which was for a  cake shop that i thought was very cool  was for charity uh every single one  i think we raised in total across  everything  probably about fifty thousand dollars  this month which is  pretty [ __ ] cool and i feel like it's  just smarter if i  figure out a way to use any income that  comes from twitch  to further those courses as someone who  is not a professional content creator or  full-time content creator and does not  do this as a way to make money it's like  that doesn't mean i can't be smarter  about it um i don't know how that's  going to look because i don't know what  taxes are going to look like  and i do really want to pay my team of  mods who on twitch are very wonderful  so i don't know what that is going to be  i don't know how much money i will make  if really any  i'm really not sure still very new to  twitch don't know how it works but that  was kind of my thought process that  there's a lot of good that can be done  out of monetizing streaming which is  something that i have not done at all  up until this point now related to me  not being a professional content creator  or full-time content creator whatsoever  this won't actually  really change anything this won't change  the frequency which width i stream  um it's not going to make me have  scheduled streams i might tell people  like the day before but a thing that's  very important to me as someone who  has a job that is quite challenging and  quite demanding and that i absolutely  love  is that i don't want to tie myself to a  schedule in case there's a really big  work day where i'm just too tired  afterwards um  none of that stuff is going to change  i'm not going to become more of a  professional streamer by any means so i  still won't be scheduling when i'm  streaming uh it's just kind of a thing  that if you follow me on twitch  i just kind of do it some days try to do  twice a week generally  but if i'm not feeling it or i'm too  busy that's the reality of that  so i don't want the partner status to  change people's expectations from me  because i am still  not a streamer by which i mean  professional streamer obviously that is  still  not me not something i ever want to do  will ever do i have absolutely no desire  to do it as anything other than a hobby  i have absolutely no desire to do it  full-time or professionally  ever so i don't want people to have that  expectation and i am a little bit  concerned about that but yeah  realistically  it'll still be streaming the same amount  which is generally like twice a week one  thing that i think will change in a  positive way  is being a little bit more integrated  into the twitch community is that i have  a lot of friends who twitch stream all  the time  and previously like i've not been able  to do any of the squad stream stuff i've  not been eligible for a lot of twitch  campaigns  um because even though i have i guess  113 000 followers thank you everyone  i'm still not a partner or even an  affiliate so there's a lot of things  that i've been borrowed from  um that should maybe involve some more  cool collaboration stuff with other  people on the platform i'm definitely  planning to  do more recurring streams with friends  um and yeah squad streaming stuff that i  feel like i've always been missing out  on which is kind of a bummer but that's  mostly it i'm very excited about it  i'm really excited about the idea of  emotes  uh my mods have already been kind of  throwing some ideas at me and i think  that'll be a really fun  opportunity to hire a cool artist and  make cool stuff  for anyone who's subscribed i don't know  that i'll do the monthly newsletters  thing it's it's not something i'm trying  to even  incentivize you towards really if  anything i would probably just like tell  people  in advance what charity i might be  raising money for that that month or  something along those lines but that is  that is part of it that  definitely does appeal to me is i feel  like it opens up some some cool  opportunities  but generally yes um i think it'll make  my youtube channel better  and less of a mess and less just like a  bunch of long streams that a lot of the  time i unlist anyway  there are still some things that i will  definitely stream on youtube and not on  twitch occasionally  um like play watch listen live will  always be on youtube because the podcast  is on youtube  any of the like journalist reviewer kind  of streams that i've done  um which are like the last of us review  chat and i did one for  cyberpunk i did too for cyberpunk  actually people's impressions planning  to do one for one division  this saturday um anything that's very  editorial  will still live on youtube because i  feel like that kind of informative  content is youtube content whereas the  gameplay stuff will stick  to twitch i think that's pretty much it  i'm very excited i hope you'll  join me over on twitch if that's the  thing you're excited about i don't have  any plans for the look to change  but i have like sub counters or any of  that kind of stuff i'm still going to  keep it very  low-fi cause i don't know what i'm doing  is the truth but i'm excited to do it  and i think we can uh make some cool  stuff happen  on the platform and and yeah i look  forward to  to beginning this journey what's up come  hang out twitch.tv such carolinas are  if you aren't already over there my chat  is a fun time  play any kind of game at any point in  time obviously this was the  five and a half hour stream and i think  the one before that valheim was a pretty  long stream too  i also for anyone who has not been uh  following me on twitch actually have  done a bunch of twitch exclusive streams  i've done podcasts that are only on  twitch  and editing videos that are only on  twitch so sometimes if i'm editing  something like editing a video i'll  stream it to twitch as well at the same  time  so i do actually already kind of do more  streams on twitch that don't exist on  youtube um that are kind of just for  things that are more casual because  again i just have this this vision of  these two platforms as being very  different kinds of content so yeah  that's it for me today everyone i look  forward to seeing you there  i'm lana i'll see you guys next time bye

